WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.404 --> 00:00:04.106
to live is really strong here

00:00:04.373 --> 00:00:05.307
for their country and for their

00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:06.141
children's future.

00:00:06.809 --> 00:00:08.877
Meantime, on the battlefield,

00:00:09.311 --> 00:00:10.112
Ukrainians say that Russian

00:00:10.379 --> 00:00:12.147
forces near the key southern

00:00:12.414 --> 00:00:14.783
city of kherson are now dug in

00:00:15.317 --> 00:00:18.020
three layers deep against

00:00:18.387 --> 00:00:18.921
unanticipated Ukrainian counter

00:00:19.321 --> 00:00:19.354
offensive.

00:00:19.621 --> 00:00:20.823
Kherson is the only regional

00:00:21.323 --> 00:00:22.224
capital that Moscow has managed

00:00:22.491 --> 00:00:24.159
to capture since it's February

00:00:24.426 --> 00:00:24.593
invasion.

00:00:25.794 --> 00:00:26.428
And the fate of the city is

00:00:26.695 --> 00:00:27.796
extremely significant for both

00:00:28.197 --> 00:00:28.297
sides.

00:00:28.831 --> 00:00:30.866
It's hard to get a real sense

00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:32.201
of the set a play on the ground

00:00:32.468 --> 00:00:33.335
this grinding war.

00:00:33.769 --> 00:00:35.871
So let's get inside from former

00:00:36.238 --> 00:00:37.339
U.S. Joint chiefs chairman the

00:00:37.439 --> 00:00:39.341
retired admiral Mike mullen and

00:00:39.341 --> 00:00:40.809
the former deputy nato

00:00:41.343 --> 00:00:42.110
commander general Richard

00:00:42.377 --> 00:00:42.511
sheriff.

00:00:42.811 --> 00:00:44.279
Welcome back to our program,

00:00:44.546 --> 00:00:45.347
both of you.

00:00:45.914 --> 00:00:48.083
I just wondered if you could

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.118
perhaps just weigh in on really

00:00:50.385 --> 00:00:52.120
the spirit that was --

00:00:52.821 --> 00:00:54.189
that we saw when we met those

00:00:54.456 --> 00:00:55.357
people in irpin.

00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:57.359
That's the bucha district.

00:00:57.459 --> 00:00:58.193
They couldn't have suffered

00:00:58.460 --> 00:00:59.361
worse pain.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:01.830
And yet, you see these people

00:01:02.197 --> 00:01:04.299
who are nowhere near giving up.

00:01:04.766 --> 00:01:06.235
Admiral mullen, what do you

00:01:06.502 --> 00:01:06.602
think?

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:08.270
&gt;&gt; I agree, Christiane.

00:01:08.537 --> 00:01:10.806
At the peace as an awful lot

00:01:11.373 --> 00:01:12.274
and is really uplifting in

00:01:12.541 --> 00:01:13.775
terms of the spirit, the

00:01:14.176 --> 00:01:15.377
determination in the

00:01:15.444 --> 00:01:15.644
resilience.

00:01:15.911 --> 00:01:18.914
Even as Putin and the Russian

00:01:19.381 --> 00:01:20.782
military have taken this

00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:23.852
different tack to try to put

00:01:24.253 --> 00:01:26.188
them out of power at a really

00:01:26.455 --> 00:01:28.090
critical time.

00:01:28.857 --> 00:01:30.792
They see me bouncing back from

00:01:31.393 --> 00:01:31.560
that.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.160
So I would --

00:01:32.794 --> 00:01:36.198
I take great hope or I have

00:01:36.465 --> 00:01:38.800
great hope for the future with

00:01:39.401 --> 00:01:40.135
respect to where this

00:01:40.402 --> 00:01:41.403
eventually goes.

00:01:41.837 --> 00:01:43.805
Because of that incredible

00:01:44.206 --> 00:01:45.407
resolve that --

00:01:45.407 --> 00:01:46.808
the depth of the people of

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:47.609
Ukraine.

00:01:47.609 --> 00:01:48.343
Not just their military but of

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:49.811
the people in the political

00:01:50.178 --> 00:01:52.080
will that's behind it.

00:01:52.814 --> 00:01:55.083
&gt;&gt; General, each of those

00:01:55.417 --> 00:01:56.818
civilians who I talked to say

00:01:57.419 --> 00:01:58.320
that their spirit and whatever

00:01:58.587 --> 00:02:00.122
they do in the --

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:03.425
is all designed to support the

00:02:03.425 --> 00:02:04.326
military who's fighting for

00:02:04.593 --> 00:02:06.161
them in the trenches and in the

00:02:06.428 --> 00:02:08.196
mud and in the cold right now.

00:02:08.463 --> 00:02:10.232
What do you think, knowing the

00:02:10.499 --> 00:02:11.833
European battleground and the

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.169
battlefield, what do you think

00:02:14.436 --> 00:02:15.837
this national spirit means on

00:02:16.204 --> 00:02:18.073
the front lines?

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:21.810
&gt;&gt; Ultimately, firstly, one has

00:02:22.177 --> 00:02:24.079
to marvel and be just full of

00:02:24.346 --> 00:02:25.781
respect and admiration for the

00:02:26.181 --> 00:02:28.317
spirit that your conversations

00:02:28.584 --> 00:02:28.884
have demonstrated.

00:02:29.451 --> 00:02:31.453
This demonstrates of the iron

00:02:31.453 --> 00:02:32.821
will and determination of the

00:02:33.455 --> 00:02:34.156
Ukrainians to defeat the

00:02:34.423 --> 00:02:34.590
Russians.

00:02:34.856 --> 00:02:37.459
And as military history shows

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:39.127
again and again to --

00:02:39.461 --> 00:02:41.063
the more lists or the --

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:44.466
the Ukrainians will do with the

00:02:44.733 --> 00:02:46.068
Russians are on the back foot.

00:02:46.335 --> 00:02:48.837
But it absolutely behooves us

00:02:49.471 --> 00:02:50.806
all in the west to continue to

00:02:51.473 --> 00:02:52.374
give the Ukrainians the support

00:02:52.641 --> 00:02:54.810
they need, the support they

00:02:55.477 --> 00:02:55.611
deserve.

00:02:55.611 --> 00:02:56.278
If we can give them the tools

00:02:56.545 --> 00:02:58.146
to do the job, I am convinced

00:02:58.413 --> 00:02:59.081
that they will do the job.

00:02:59.748 --> 00:03:03.485
In that spirit will shine

00:03:03.619 --> 00:03:03.752
through.

00:03:04.019 --> 00:03:06.154
&gt;&gt; I'm just going to point out

00:03:06.421 --> 00:03:08.023
that you are wearing the red

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:08.390
poppy.

00:03:08.657 --> 00:03:10.826
It's the annual symbol of

00:03:11.493 --> 00:03:11.693
armistice day.

00:03:11.693 --> 00:03:13.061
At the end of the war that the

00:03:13.495 --> 00:03:15.797
British and commonwealth troops

00:03:16.164 --> 00:03:16.198
--

00:03:16.465 --> 00:03:17.933
they celebrate and they

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:18.500
commemorate.

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:19.501
So it's an important moment

00:03:19.635 --> 00:03:20.068
right now.

00:03:20.335 --> 00:03:21.503
All these years since the end

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.138
of the two world wars in

00:03:23.505 --> 00:03:23.538
Europe.

00:03:23.805 --> 00:03:25.907
Let's talk about kherson and

00:03:26.274 --> 00:03:27.876
let me ask you both what you

00:03:28.276 --> 00:03:32.814
make of this slow but somewhat

00:03:33.515 --> 00:03:34.116
methodical activity in and

00:03:34.383 --> 00:03:35.517
around kherson.

00:03:35.784 --> 00:03:38.820
Admiral mullen, can I ask you

00:03:39.187 --> 00:03:40.122
what you think is going on

00:03:40.389 --> 00:03:42.224
there in terms of what we hear

00:03:42.491 --> 00:03:44.826
the Russians say that asking or

00:03:45.193 --> 00:03:46.395
telling citizens and civilians

00:03:46.662 --> 00:03:47.529
to move out.

00:03:47.929 --> 00:03:49.531
They say, Alicia crews are

00:03:49.531 --> 00:03:50.399
pointing out, that they're now

00:03:50.666 --> 00:03:52.100
dug in several layers deep.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:55.537
What do you think one can

00:03:55.704 --> 00:03:55.837
expect?

00:03:56.104 --> 00:03:57.806
&gt;&gt; Christiane, several months

00:03:58.173 --> 00:03:59.808
ago, all of us were talking

00:04:00.175 --> 00:04:01.543
about getting to some version

00:04:01.543 --> 00:04:02.244
of a stalemate.

00:04:02.778 --> 00:04:04.780
Certainly that was as winter

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:05.547
approached.

00:04:06.014 --> 00:04:07.816
I had several people tell me in

00:04:08.183 --> 00:04:09.818
September that winter had

00:04:10.185 --> 00:04:11.787
already arrived from the

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:13.555
fighting standpoint and that

00:04:13.655 --> 00:04:15.057
clearly has not been the case.

00:04:15.757 --> 00:04:17.826
The Ukrainians continue to make

00:04:18.193 --> 00:04:18.360
progress.

00:04:18.627 --> 00:04:20.829
But literally since Kyiv, the

00:04:21.196 --> 00:04:22.831
lines of communication, the

00:04:23.198 --> 00:04:24.132
logistics challenge.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:26.802
The battlefield challenge has

00:04:27.202 --> 00:04:27.569
just --

00:04:27.602 --> 00:04:28.170
they've been extended.

00:04:28.437 --> 00:04:31.073
And so the further east that

00:04:31.573 --> 00:04:33.208
the Ukrainians go, I think the

00:04:33.575 --> 00:04:34.176
tougher the fight.

00:04:34.443 --> 00:04:36.111
And certainly kurson as the

00:04:36.378 --> 00:04:38.780
regional capital will be

00:04:39.181 --> 00:04:39.981
significant.

00:04:40.248 --> 00:04:42.184
Not just physically significant

00:04:42.451 --> 00:04:43.785
but I think really significant

00:04:44.186 --> 00:04:45.587
as to the eventual outcome.

00:04:45.987 --> 00:04:48.123
I think the more Ukraine

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.092
reaches to the east.

00:04:50.358 --> 00:04:51.026
The tough for the fight is

00:04:51.593 --> 00:04:51.760
going to be.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:52.794
Much less in the middle of the

00:04:53.195 --> 00:04:55.063
winter which is obviously now

00:04:55.597 --> 00:04:56.064
setting in.

00:04:56.331 --> 00:04:57.799
I think we can expect a very,

00:04:58.166 --> 00:05:00.135
very difficult battle.

00:05:00.769 --> 00:05:03.171
To come and in --

00:05:03.605 --> 00:05:04.840
the next few weeks and months

00:05:05.207 --> 00:05:09.044
with kherson and very much in

00:05:09.611 --> 00:05:09.878
the middle of it.

00:05:09.878 --> 00:05:12.247
&gt;&gt; General, what is the value,

00:05:12.514 --> 00:05:14.182
the strategic value of kherson.

00:05:14.449 --> 00:05:15.217
Apart from the fact that the

00:05:15.617 --> 00:05:17.252
Russians took it practically on

00:05:17.619 --> 00:05:17.652
day one.

00:05:17.919 --> 00:05:19.187
It's the only major city that

00:05:19.621 --> 00:05:19.688
they've taken.

00:05:19.955 --> 00:05:21.089
And they're desperate to hold

00:05:21.623 --> 00:05:21.790
on to it.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:24.793
Its position is crucial for

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:25.627
both sides.

00:05:25.627 --> 00:05:27.095
&gt;&gt; Exactly that.

00:05:27.763 --> 00:05:28.029
It's --

00:05:28.296 --> 00:05:30.031
losing kherson would be a

00:05:30.298 --> 00:05:31.099
humiliation for Putin.

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:34.202
But the kherson is the key to

00:05:34.469 --> 00:05:35.137
the black sea coastline.

00:05:35.837 --> 00:05:37.906
And if the Ukrainians regain

00:05:38.306 --> 00:05:39.775
kherson, then the Russians are

00:05:40.175 --> 00:05:41.076
going to be pushed back to the

00:05:41.643 --> 00:05:43.044
west into the eastern side of

00:05:43.311 --> 00:05:44.146
the dnipro.

00:05:44.412 --> 00:05:47.849
And that gives Ukraine access

00:05:48.216 --> 00:05:49.217
again to the black sea.

00:05:49.851 --> 00:05:51.286
That means that they're not

00:05:51.653 --> 00:05:53.822
just dependent on Odessa to get

00:05:54.222 --> 00:05:55.323
there or grain, they're steel

00:05:55.657 --> 00:05:56.391
out to the rest of the world

00:05:56.658 --> 00:05:57.793
they can use other ports as

00:05:58.193 --> 00:05:58.293
well.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.829
Kherson is of strategic

00:06:01.196 --> 00:06:01.663
importance.

00:06:01.663 --> 00:06:03.832
&gt;&gt; I want to ask you both

00:06:04.199 --> 00:06:05.100
because what we seem to have

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:07.836
seen is a subtle and not so

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:09.171
subtle shift in the balance of

00:06:09.671 --> 00:06:10.105
artillery power.

00:06:10.772 --> 00:06:13.241
Maybe not physical numbers in

00:06:13.675 --> 00:06:15.243
terms of man but certainly in

00:06:15.677 --> 00:06:17.813
the effectiveness of what the

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.014
Ukrainians are using.

00:06:19.281 --> 00:06:20.782
Thanks to all the nato

00:06:21.183 --> 00:06:22.017
equipment that is coming in.

00:06:22.784 --> 00:06:24.853
It was reported in one of the

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.822
newspapers that a Ukrainian

00:06:27.189 --> 00:06:28.857
commander on the ground

00:06:29.224 --> 00:06:31.760
basically said that if the

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.161
Russians, as sort of

00:06:33.695 --> 00:06:34.763
ill-equipped as they are right

00:06:35.163 --> 00:06:36.198
now, hang on to kherson.

00:06:36.464 --> 00:06:38.233
It could be their stalingrad.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.102
I just wondered admiral mullen

00:06:41.369 --> 00:06:43.038
what you make of how the

00:06:43.305 --> 00:06:45.040
Ukrainians are using all of

00:06:45.307 --> 00:06:46.341
this new kit that is coming in.

00:06:46.775 --> 00:06:48.844
And what more do you think they

00:06:49.211 --> 00:06:49.311
need?

00:06:49.711 --> 00:06:50.779
&gt;&gt; I think they've been

00:06:51.146 --> 00:06:53.081
extraordinary in terms of their

00:06:53.348 --> 00:06:54.216
ability to respond.

00:06:55.817 --> 00:06:57.819
I was very happy to see

00:06:58.186 --> 00:06:59.354
reported publicly in the last

00:06:59.721 --> 00:07:02.123
day or two that the air defense

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:04.826
systems, I think one from the

00:07:05.193 --> 00:07:07.229
U.S. And one from Spain, have a

00:07:07.729 --> 00:07:07.896
arrived.

00:07:07.896 --> 00:07:08.797
Because that's not an

00:07:09.164 --> 00:07:10.031
insignificant threat as well.

00:07:10.298 --> 00:07:11.833
And supporting them in that

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:12.334
regard.

00:07:12.601 --> 00:07:14.302
In addition to the systems that

00:07:14.569 --> 00:07:15.303
we've provided thus far.

00:07:15.804 --> 00:07:17.839
Plus the intelligence sharing

00:07:18.206 --> 00:07:19.975
that we clearly have provided.

00:07:20.242 --> 00:07:22.777
I think in a way, it gets this

00:07:23.178 --> 00:07:23.745
black sea issue.

00:07:24.012 --> 00:07:26.147
I think if Putin loses control

00:07:26.414 --> 00:07:28.116
of the black sea, you can

00:07:28.383 --> 00:07:30.151
almost say that he's lost the

00:07:30.418 --> 00:07:30.485
war.

00:07:30.752 --> 00:07:31.786
It is one of the reasons he

00:07:32.153 --> 00:07:34.289
took crimea originally so that

00:07:34.556 --> 00:07:36.124
he wasn't going to lose his

00:07:36.391 --> 00:07:37.192
fleet capabilities.

00:07:37.759 --> 00:07:39.261
Navy fleet capability.

00:07:40.795 --> 00:07:42.097
I think we do, as it gets

00:07:42.364 --> 00:07:44.199
harder and harder financially

00:07:44.466 --> 00:07:46.101
for many countries to support.

00:07:46.368 --> 00:07:47.202
I think we also need to keep in

00:07:47.769 --> 00:07:49.237
mind how vital that the lane is

00:07:49.771 --> 00:07:52.908
to support the food issues that

00:07:53.275 --> 00:07:53.875
are throughout the globe right

00:07:54.276 --> 00:07:55.076
now because of this war.

00:07:55.343 --> 00:07:56.278
There are many countries that

00:07:56.544 --> 00:07:57.812
were on edge before the war

00:07:58.179 --> 00:07:59.781
started in terms of food

00:08:00.181 --> 00:08:00.782
insecurity and that has been

00:08:01.182 --> 00:08:02.217
badly exacerbated.

00:08:02.484 --> 00:08:05.820
In a way, it really is kherson

00:08:06.254 --> 00:08:07.422
has the possibility of being a

00:08:07.789 --> 00:08:09.824
real standoff position at that

00:08:10.225 --> 00:08:11.259
can turn the outcome of this

00:08:11.793 --> 00:08:12.360
war one way or the other.

00:08:12.761 --> 00:08:15.096
Then lastly, as it turns

00:08:15.363 --> 00:08:16.064
against --

00:08:16.331 --> 00:08:17.966
continues to turn against Putin.

00:08:18.233 --> 00:08:19.834
My biggest worry is that

00:08:20.235 --> 00:08:21.803
somehow being desperate and

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:23.104
losing, he'll turn to the use

00:08:23.371 --> 00:08:24.139
of nuclear weapons.

00:08:24.406 --> 00:08:25.840
Which I think changes

00:08:26.207 --> 00:08:26.408
everything.

00:08:26.675 --> 00:08:28.076
We need to figure out as best

00:08:28.343 --> 00:08:29.811
we can how that could never

00:08:30.178 --> 00:08:30.312
happen.

00:08:30.578 --> 00:08:31.813
And that's a very complex and

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.149
difficult task as well.

00:08:34.416 --> 00:08:36.785
&gt;&gt; I'm going to get to that in

00:08:37.185 --> 00:08:37.852
a moment because obviously it

00:08:38.219 --> 00:08:40.155
is the big thing that worries

00:08:40.422 --> 00:08:41.222
and scares everybody.

00:08:41.489 --> 00:08:42.357
But let me just ask you.

00:08:42.791 --> 00:08:43.291
You are an admiral.

00:08:43.825 --> 00:08:45.160
You understand better than any

00:08:45.427 --> 00:08:48.096
of us the sea, the war on the

00:08:48.363 --> 00:08:49.364
sea and the laws of the sea.

00:08:49.831 --> 00:08:50.832
You saw that the Ukrainians are

00:08:51.199 --> 00:08:53.902
used to suicide drones against

00:08:54.302 --> 00:08:57.839
parts of that fleet that you're

00:08:58.173 --> 00:08:58.406
talking about.

00:08:58.673 --> 00:08:58.707
--

00:08:58.974 --> 00:08:59.140
in crimea.

00:08:59.841 --> 00:09:01.876
How important is that and then

00:09:02.277 --> 00:09:03.144
given what you just said about

00:09:03.411 --> 00:09:05.847
the vital nature of that whole

00:09:06.181 --> 00:09:07.182
coastline for Russia.

00:09:07.849 --> 00:09:09.184
What more damage do you think

00:09:09.451 --> 00:09:11.386
the Ukrainians could do there?

00:09:11.853 --> 00:09:15.190
&gt;&gt; As I understand it, I think

00:09:15.457 --> 00:09:15.924
the Russians and move their

00:09:16.191 --> 00:09:17.125
fleet basically out of range.

00:09:17.859 --> 00:09:18.293
Certainly of the kind of

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:19.260
Michelin where the --

00:09:19.861 --> 00:09:22.831
if I look at that and I look at

00:09:23.198 --> 00:09:24.799
the recent action with respect

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.201
to the Ukrainians impacting.

00:09:26.468 --> 00:09:27.235
I'd say the Russian fleet is

00:09:27.502 --> 00:09:28.203
pretty vulnerable.

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:29.404
I don't know that they could

00:09:29.871 --> 00:09:33.008
hold up very well in a kind of

00:09:33.274 --> 00:09:33.441
conflict.

00:09:33.875 --> 00:09:34.309
It's almost --

00:09:34.809 --> 00:09:35.877
it's an asymmetric

00:09:36.277 --> 00:09:36.511
vulnerability.

00:09:36.978 --> 00:09:38.213
I would expect the Ukrainians

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:40.815
to continue or certainly to

00:09:41.182 --> 00:09:42.083
support that.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.284
Obviously, the Russians will

00:09:43.551 --> 00:09:45.220
use that fleet as much as they

00:09:45.487 --> 00:09:48.790
can to control both access and

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.058
trade in and out of the black

00:09:50.325 --> 00:09:50.392
sea.

